# unseen-conv-configs -- curated convolution problems deliberately NOT present in
# tier1-conv-configs, used to measure generalization to never-encountered
# problems (quick-tuning / ML-classifier coverage on out-of-distribution shapes).
# Each line is fully specified (op/dtype token, -F direction, -f/-I/-O layouts)
# so it maps to exactly one problem with no combinatorial expansion.
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored by the config loader.
#
# Novelty is anchored on axes tier1 never exercises:
#   * bf16 (convbfp16) -- tier1 has only f32/f16/i8
#   * backward-weights (-F 4 / wrw) -- tier1 has only -F 1 (fwd) and -F 2 (bwd-data)
#   * dilation > 1 (-l/-j > 1) -- tier1 is dilation 1 everywhere
#   * fresh / unaligned shapes and novel group counts (4, 8, 16, 32)

# --- bf16 forward: an entirely unseen datatype ---
